Ravines (11.3 km)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/events/316563686/","description":"Join us on this hike to Humber Bay Shores Farmers Market, taking place in the picturesque Humber Bay Park West. It's the final one of the season. You'll find an incredible variety of farm-fresh produce, baked goods, artisanal products, preserves, meats, and more, all sourced from the city and surrounding regions. The market is a staple of the community, fostering engagement and supporting local agriculture.\n\nAfter the market, we will head east over the Humber Bay Arch Bridge to High Park and through its ravines, ending at Keele Station. Those who want a sit-down meal can continue east on Bloor St for Ukrainian syrnyky (cheese pancakes), deruny (potato pancakes), green borscht, and varenyky (dumplings).\n\n**Highlights**\n\n1. Old Mill subway station (depart 10:30am)\n2. Old Mill\n3. Humber River Recreational Trail\n4. Oculus Pavilion\n5. Floating bridge over Humber Bay wetlands\n6. Humber Bay Shores Farmers' Market\n7. Views of CN Tower and downtown Toronto\n8. Humber Bay Arch Bridge\n9. Grenadier Pond\n10. Spring Creek\n11. Bloor and Keele (arrive 1:45pm)\n\n**Neighbourhoods**\nThe Kingsway > Sunnylea > Stonegate-Queensway > Humber Bay Shores > Sunnyside > High Park\n\n**Map**\n[https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=12q2PqID-bXHnS1prfD9QVvxdc3tWhTE&usp=sharing](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=12q2PqID-bXHnS1prfD9QVvxdc3tWhTE&usp=sharing)\n\nUnpaved and narrow trails in High Park.\n\n**How it works**\nThere are no scheduled checkpoints for this hike. If late, you can try to find us at the farmers market. Bus 66B goes to the market from Old Mill Station.\n\nSee our [homepage](https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/) for more info.","startDate":"2026-10-10T14:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Old Mill subway station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"2676 Bloor Street West, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Hike to Eat","url":"https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/"},"performer":"Hike to Eat"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Salmon Run @ Etienne Brulé Park","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/events/316437292/","description":"Ready to witness a natural wonder right here in the city?\n\nJoin us for a chill walk to see the **salmon run** at Etienne Brulé Park! We'll meet up at **Etienne Brulé Park Parking** and take a stroll along the Humber River, where we'll watch the salmon jump and splash their way upstream.\nIt's a sight you won't want to miss!\n\nAfter our walk, let's grab a coffee and a snack to relax and chat about what we saw. It's the perfect way to spend an afternoon and connect with fellow nature lovers.\n\n**Meeting spot:** Etienne Brulé Park Parking lot\n**What to bring:** Just comfy shoes and a sense of adventure!\n\n$2 event fee, cash at the event or etransfer: mech.mandeep@gmail.com","startDate":"2026-10-10T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Etienne Brulé Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"4-6 Catherine St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe & Wander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/"},"performer":"Vibe & Wander"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Founders and Entrepreneurs Networking at 5 Elements Espresso Bar","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-founders-hub/events/315547597/","description":"Join the Toronto Founders Hub every other Saturday at 3:30pm for our regular meetup at 5 Elements Espresso Bar.\n\nSit down with other entrepreneurs to network and discuss business ideas or strategies.\n\\- Broaden your network\n\\- Get critical feedback\n\\- Socialize in low pressure setting\n\nI look forward to seeing you!","startDate":"2026-10-10T19:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"5 Elements Espresso","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"131 Avenue Road, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Founders and Entrepreneurs Hub","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-founders-hub/"},"performer":"Toronto Founders and Entrepreneurs Hub"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Coffee meetup for shy and socially anxious people","url":"https://www.meetup.com/social-anxiety-and-general-anxiety-group/events/312664385/","description":"Our coffee shop meetup now takes place every other Saturday. Come out to meet and chat with your fellow members of the Toronto Social Anxiety Support group in a supportive environment.\n\n**IMPORTANT: This group is intended to provide a safe space for people with social anxiety who may feel inhibited in louder, more extroverted environments. Please respect the nature of this group and do not attend if you are not in this category. There are many other groups available on Meetup.**\n\n**When**: 5pm - 7pm\n\n**Where to meet**: Alternity Café, just west of St. George Street, on the south side of Bloor. Vegan café with a chill vibe. Here is their website: https://alternity.ca/pages/our-place\n\n**Reminder**: Like all our events, the group's code of conduct applies. Pls make this a successful outing by being courteous and respectful in language and behaviour, and supportive towards other members, especially those with higher anxiety.\n\n**Covid/flu safety**: If you are sick or have recently been exposed to someone who is sick, pls use your judgement about attending this event. You can always come to the next event when you feel better.","startDate":"2026-10-10T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Alternity","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"333 Bloor st west Toronto,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Shyness, Social Anxiety and General Anxiety Support Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/social-anxiety-and-general-anxiety-group/"},"performer":"Shyness, Social Anxiety and General Anxiety Support Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":" Fast Friends: Meet New People, Make Connections & Play 50+ Board Games | 25–45","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-singles-in-the-city/events/316554958/","description":"Looking for a better way to spend a Saturday evening in Toronto than sitting at home wondering how to expand your social circle?\n\nFast Friends gives you an easy starting point. Instead of walking into a busy pub and hoping you happen to meet the right people, our host creates the structure — guiding conversations and rotations so you can meet a variety of people naturally, even if you arrive on your own.\n\nAnd this time, we’re back at Stout Irish Pub — a relaxed Toronto pub where the socialising can continue long after the hosted rounds finish, with drinks, food and 50+ board games to choose from. 🎲🍻\n\n🎟️ Book Early & Save: [https://toronto10thoct.eventbrite.co.uk](https://toronto10thoct.eventbrite.co.uk)\n\nYou can pay securely online with any debit or credit card through PayPal — no PayPal account required.\n*Advance tickets are cheaper and help us plan the right space and group size for a comfortable evening.*\n\nEarly Bird: CAD $10 \\| Regular: CAD $15 \\| At the Door: CAD $20 cash\n\n🤝 The Evening\n7:00 PM — Welcome & Settle In\nMeet your host, Kristabelle, grab a drink and get comfortable.\nWhether you've just moved to Toronto or have been here for years, this is a chance to step out of your usual routine and meet some different people.\nComing alone? That's completely fine — most guests do.\n\n7:30–8:30 PM — Fast Friends\nForget the usual “How do I start talking to someone?” moment.\nOur host guides a series of short conversations and rotations, giving you the chance to meet different people throughout the evening. You don't need to plan what happens next — just show up, join the conversation and see who you connect with.\n\n✨ Themed Connection Rounds\nWe'll mix things up with interactive prompts and themed conversation challenges that help uncover common interests and unexpected connections.\nFrom travel and food to music, books, hobbies and weekend adventures, these rounds are designed to get you talking about something more interesting than small talk.\n\n🎲 8:30 PM onwards — 50+ Board Games & Socialising\nThis is where Stout really adds something special.\nOnce the hosted rounds finish, you don't have to call it a night. Stout has 50+ board games available, giving you an easy way to continue socialising with the people you've just met.\nPick a game, join a group, grab another drink, or simply keep chatting. You can make the evening as relaxed and spontaneous as you like.\n\n❤️ Why Come Along?\n✔️ Meet 20+ new people in one evening\n✔️ Guided conversations make it easier to connect\n✔️ Interactive themed rounds to spark better conversations\n✔️ 50+ board games at Stout 🎲\n✔️ Relaxed Irish pub atmosphere\n✔️ Reserved space for our group\n✔️ Members from our Toronto Meetup communities may also join\n✔️ Most guests come solo\n✔️ Designed for ladies and gents aged 25–45\n✔️ Friendship-focused — not a dating event\n\n📍 Why Stout Irish Pub?\nLocated at 221 Carlton Street, Stout is an easy-to-reach Toronto pub with a relaxed atmosphere, drinks, food and one of the best extras for a social event — a huge selection of 50+ board games.\nSo you can start the evening with structured conversations and finish it however you want: playing, chatting, laughing or getting to know someone you clicked with.\n\n👥 Who Is It For?\nYou don't need to be new to Toronto, part of an existing group or know anyone attending.\nIf your social circle could use some fresh faces — whether you're new in town or simply ready to meet people outside your usual routine — you're welcome.\n\nCome by yourself, bring a friend, or do both.\n\n🌍 About Fast Friends\nFor over 10 years, Fast Friends has been creating opportunities for people to connect through professionally hosted social events in 30+ cities worldwide.\n\nOur goal is simple: make meeting people easier and give you a reason to actually start the conversation.\nCome solo. We'll guide the experience. You make the connections. ❤️","startDate":"2026-10-10T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Stout Irish pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"221 Carlton St., Toronto, ON M5A 2L2, Canada,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Singles in the city (13000+)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-singles-in-the-city/"},"performer":"Toronto Singles in the city (13000+)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto’s BIGGEST Language Exchange Social Event Party + Bonus Class by [TILE.]","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tilesocial/events/316527539/","description":"**Join [TILE.]** at the **most popular Saturday Language Learning Social Event & Party in Toronto! 🍁**\n\n**[TILE.] = Toronto International Language Exchange [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/tilelearning/) & [Website](https://www.tilelearning.com/)**\n\n**[TILE.]** now has a **2-for-1 special event,** which includes:\n**1.** From **[6:30 - 7:15 PM](https://www.meetup.com/english-class-with-certified-award-winning-teacher):** An optional $5 small group 45-minute **[English language class](https://www.meetup.com/english-class-with-certified-award-winning-teacher)** taught by an award-winning certified language teacher with 10+ years experience (OCT, University of Toronto PhD researcher, MA, BEd & HBA)\n\n**2.** From **[7:15 - 11 PM](https://www.meetup.com/biggest-language-party-event-social-in-toronto):** Our usual huge group **[BIGGEST LANGUAGE EXCHANGE SOCIAL EVENT AND PARTY IN TORONTO](https://www.meetup.com/biggest-language-party-event-social-in-toronto)** (Cost: *$5, unless you already paid for the same day 6:30 English class right before, in which which case the 7:15 social is FREE)*\n\nBoth events happen Saturday on the 2nd floor of the Madison Pub (14 Madison Avenue). ***Attend either or both events for $5!***\n\n**Join us for:**\n**✅ 💬🌎🎉 Language Exchanges and Learning in a Fun Setting**\n**✅ 🤝🗣️🥳 Meeting New Friends & Networking**\n**✅ 🃏🎲 🂱 Group Games & Activities**\n**✅ 🎸🎤🎧 Bonus Multilingual Music (on special event days)**\n**✅ 💃🎵🕺 (Post-event) on-site Madison Pub Dancing, Piano Bar, Singing & More!**\n**✅🍔🍺🍟 On-site Appetizers, Drinks and Food for Purchase at the Bar & Restaurant**\n\nGet your Ticket at the door OR buy a [$5 digital ticket online here](https://www.tilelearning.com/events).\n\nMeet Toronto locals and international friends. Talk to language teachers and speakers to learn English, French, Korean, Japanese, Spanish, and much more! Join us for board games, conversation, dancing, singing, and more! Make sure to get a nametag from one of our helpers.\n\n*You **must** read the full event description below before attending. By attending, you agree to all the terms listed.*\n\n**[TILE.] Toronto International Language Exchange** event details:\n\n* We are on the 2nd floor of the Madison pub on the patio with all the international flags! *The dance floor opens around 10 PM, and the live piano bar singer start around 10:30 on the 1st floor.*\n\n**PAY** **$5** right at the event by **CASH, CREDIT, or DEBIT**, or **SEND $5 E-TRANSFERS** to: **JOHN@TILELEARNING.COM**. You can also support the bar by buying a drink or appetizer.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**IMPORTANT DISCLAIMER – Meetup Group**\nBy attending any TILE events, including these ones, you acknowledge and agree to the following:\n\n* *The organizers and hosts of TILE events are are not liable for any loss, injury, damage, or other unforeseen outcomes that may occur before, during, or after any event.*\n* *Participation in TILE events is entirely voluntary and at your own risk. You are solely responsible for your own safety, personal belongings, transportation, behavior, and well-being. It is your responsibility to assess the risks involved in any activity or location and to act accordingly.*\n* *TILE and its organizers do not provide insurance and cannot guarantee the safety, accuracy of information, or quality of venues, third-party services, or other attendees.*\n* *By attending, you release TILE, its organizers, and affiliates from any and all claims or liability, and you agree to conduct yourself respectfully and in accordance with local laws and venue rules.*\n* ***If you do not agree with this disclaimer, please do not attend TILE events.***","startDate":"2026-10-10T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Madison Avenue Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"14 Madison Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto's BIGGEST Language Exchange Social Event + Class","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tilesocial/"},"performer":"Toronto's BIGGEST Language Exchange Social Event + Class"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Walk and Salmon watching (Free or Paid Event))","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tamclub/events/316415769/","description":"Salmons are expected to be swimming upstream. An annual upward migration. We will spend some time to watch at a few spots and then continue with our walk and return back to the starting point. We will wait until 3:10pm and start walking. If you arrive late, pls follow the Humber River Trail heading north and you can catch up with the group.\n\nDistance: 7 to 9km\n\nDifficulty: Very Easy\n\nTrail: Flat Paved Trail\n\n**Transport**\nRecommend taking TTC or Uber.\n\n**TTC**: Get off Old Mill station and walk to the park.\n\n**Parking**: There is Paid & Free Parking available nearby meeting spot. Pls look up if you are driving.\n\n**Event Fee\\***\nFree if you RSVP before Sep16\n$1.99 if you RSVP on/after Sep17\n\n**Cash** - *In person when you arrive at event*\n**Etransfer-** *[themoja@outlook.com](http://mailto:themoja@outlook.com/) --> use password **meetup***\n**Credit Card**- *[Click here to pay via Stripe](https://buy.stripe.com/bJeeVd3li4Cq3rS7Gh0oM00)*\n\n💬 **Stay Connected:**\n***Join Whatsapp Group - [CLICK HERE](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSflzD3fDrU5sLARAT5yDF3OhEu3Vj-2P7ci8mP5FYX46rt1NQ/viewform)***\n***Follow on Instagram - [CLICK HERE](https://www.instagram.com/tam.club/)***\n\n\\**Signing up in advance helps us plan better. If you’d like to join without registering, there is a $15 drop-in fee. Pls bring exact amount in cash.*","startDate":"2026-10-10T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Etienne Brule Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"13 Crosby Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Asian Meetup - TAM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tamclub/"},"performer":"Toronto Asian Meetup - TAM"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Saturday Mix, Mingle and Bowling with Friends! ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/316502324/","description":"Hello everyone,\n\nPlan to join us for a great day to Mix, Mingle and **Bowl, with optional Dinner and Live Music Party after.**\n\n**Please arrive between 4:00 pm & 4:45 pm**-so I can secure lanes for everyone\n(You will see me (Steve Flemming) (and the group) when you walk in through the front entrance in the main bar/seating area\n\\*We will have time to introduce ourselves and get to know each other before we begin the bowling :)\n\n\\*Joined by my other groups to so we can anticipate a terrific turn out.\n\n\\*Event details below\n\\-\\-\\-\n**Location:**\n**Play Time Bowl**\n33 Samor Rd, North York, ON M6A 1J2\n**Free Parking** found all around the location\n\\-\\-\\-\n\nSincerely,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n[meetup.com/soulcity/](http://meetup.com/soulcity/)\n\nEvent Details:\n**Saturday Mix, Mingle and Bowling with Friends!**\n\n\\*No experience required\n(I'm happy to help you out if you're new to bowling)\n\n-A fun, well organized event with lots of socializing, mingling and of course ten pin bowling!\n-This event is totally co-ed for all levels and all ages\n-Bring along your friends if you like or come on your own; either way we'll have a great time\n\\*We will go for dinner after as well :)\n-Free Parking as well all around the venue\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Event Fee:** 40 dollars (Includes Social Mixer, 90 minutes of Bowling, and then more mingling after (optional)\nAlso includes HST & Shoe Rental in the price)\n\\*Cash only when you arrive\nor by e transfer in advance: **[steveflemming11@gmail.com](http://steveflemming11@gmail.com)**\n\\*10 dollars if you wish to just take part in the mix/mingle part but not the bowling\n^Bonus (optional) Dinner and Live Music Party after bowling event- no extra charge-car pooling will be arranged\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Friendly Reminders:**\nLocated just south of 401 and just off of Dufferin (on west side)\n\\*Parking is Free (located on both sides of building)\nClosest subway station is Yorkdale Mall\n-10 minute walk from the mall subway station\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-","startDate":"2026-10-10T20:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Play Time Bowl","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"33 Samor, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"All-Level &Beginner Friendly $10 Drop In Saturday Morning @ CA Badminton ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/events/316332798/","description":":Saturday Morning Drop In\nCost $ 10 \\*\\*\\*\n\\* Included Plastic birdies, please try to have cash and pay before playing.\n\\*\\*\\*(Cash Only) (Cash Only) (Cash Only)\n\nLocation: 1370 Birchmount Rd, Unit 6\